{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2912","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2912","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2912\",\"parent_revision\":\"0e856aa6d61b574376a09ba3700fe8f2da2aa358\",\"root_revision\":\"cc30fcd42a074e3a47cf5292674d2d1cd97c8696038c8bc4f7a90c6068d34166\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe plugin-creator:shared-content-references skill's Technique 1 (Plugin-Root Shared Doc) prescribes writing a live markdown link like [doc](${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/<doc>.md) from a SKILL.md body to share content across 2+ skill directories in one plugin \u2014 and this substitution is independently verified to resolve correctly at runtime (see AGENTS.md's ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} substitution notes, canary-tested 2026-08-06). But uvx skilllint@latest check's InternalLinkValidator (LK001/LK002) does not resolve ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} \u2014 it checks the literal string as a filesystem path, finds nothing at './${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/...', and reports 'Broken link (file not found)' plus a spurious './ prefix' suggestion. Reproduced 2026-08-16: adding a real (non-fenced) ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/... link to claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md and claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md triggered LK001 on both; the shared-content-references skill's own SKILL.md uses the identical pattern but only inside fenced code-block examples, which InternalLinkValidator apparently skips \u2014 so this gap has never been exercised by a live link before. Worked around by using a plain relative path (../../docs/<doc>.md) instead, which works for skills at the same directory depth but doesn't have the portability/reload-safety properties ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} is supposed to provide for skills at different depths or if the skill directory structure changes. skilllint's InternalLinkValidator should special-case ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} the same way it presumably already ignores fenced-code-block examples, resolving them relative to the plugin/skill root before checking file existence.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **bug(skilllint): internallinkvalidator doesn't resolve ${claude_plugin_root} in live markdown links, flagging shared-content-references' own technique 1 as broken** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"cd1697cdc722bf12ec2bf0e8ba9b02357c8f19a288b61b39d550cdd26935d970\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTopUQ\"}"}